cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MolViewer in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
title: "MolViewer: a free, open-source 3D molecule viewer for the browser"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shulga
    given-names: Gleb
repository-code: "https://github.com/GlebShulga/molviewer"
url: "https://molviewer.bio"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  MolViewer is a free, open-source web application for viewing 3D molecular
  structures in the browser. It loads PDB entries, AlphaFold predictions and
  PubChem small molecules, opens PDB, mmCIF, SDF, MOL and XYZ files, and
  provides cartoon, ball-and-stick, spacefill and surface representations,
  secondary-structure and pLDDT coloring, distance, angle and dihedral
  measurements, multi-structure comparison, share links and embedding.
keywords:
  - molecular visualization
  - protein structure
  - PDB
  - mmCIF
  - AlphaFold
  - structural biology
  - WebGL
  - Three.js
